The generated model is structurally incorrect and requires a complete replacement. The previous patch attempt failed because it did not correctly implement the time lags and used the wrong time horizon. A correct replacement must be a faithful implementation of the reference model for the specific scenario (obj_choice=2, T=5, H=4, use_exo=0).

Replace the entire generated model and data with the following:

**Model File:**
```ampl
set I;
param T integer > 0;
param H integer >= 0 <= T;
set Y0  := 0..T+1;
set Ybal := 0..H;
set Yy  := 2..T+1;

param C  {I, I} >= 0;
param D  {I, I} >= 0;
param mx {I} >= 0;
param my {I} >= 0;
param cap0   {I} >= 0;
param stock0 {I} >= 0;
param M >= 0;

var x {i in I, t in Y0} >= 0;
var s {i in I, t in Y0} >= 0;
var y {i in I, t in Yy} >= 0;

maximize Total_Production_Last_Two_Years:
  sum {i in I} (x[i,T-1] + x[i,T]);

subject to InitStock {i in I}: s[i,0] = stock0[i];
subject to NoProductionYear0 {i in I}: x[i,0] = 0;
subject to NoCapacityAfterYearT {i in I}: y[i,T+1] = 0;

subject to CapacityLimit {i in I, t in Y0}:
  x[i,t] <= cap0[i] + sum {tt in Yy: tt <= t} y[i,tt];

subject to Balance {i in I, t in Ybal}:
  x[i,t] + s[i,t] = 0 + sum {j in I} C[i,j] * x[j,t+1] + sum {j in I} D[i,j] * (if t+2 in Yy then y[j,t+2] else 0) + s[i,t+1];

subject to ManpowerCap {t in Ybal}:
  sum {j in I} mx[j] * x[j,t+1] + sum {j in I} my[j] * (if t+2 in Yy then y[j,t+2] else 0) <= M;
```

